             redraw in game: "Behemoth (forsakendragon) is so cool it really deserves to be
             MUCH larger now. One of the most massive creatures."

             ⛔ DO NOT re-derive these from CREATURE_RESIZE_LIST.md. The list's x0.62 was
             computed from the OLD art - 1,614 px carrying a SUPER silhouette, the weakest
             headliner in the cast, shrunk to hide it. That art no longer exists: the owner
             authorised the redraw and it ships at 1,024 px. The premise of the shrink is
             gone, so the derived multiplier does not apply and its row is marked overridden.

             🔴 DOUBLED AGAIN 2026-08-24, same sitting: "double it again, AND do it for
             bodySize fully. This is now the night side's heaviest hitter and most amazing
             thing." Adult drawSize 8.00 -> 16.00, all three stages x2 again.

             ⚠️ 16.00 IS PAST WHAT THE ART SUPPORTS, KNOWINGLY, AND HE WAS TOLD. The sizing
             rule is texture edge = drawSize x 128, so 16.00 wants a 2,048 px sprite and the
             approved art is 1,024 - it renders at 64 px/cell, HALF the standard. ⛔ The fix
             is NOT to upscale the file: resampling 1024 -> 2048 adds no detail and would only
             make the number look compliant while the art stayed soft. It is to REGENERATE
             at 2,048 px, which is a new generation and needs his approval because he
             approved THIS sprite.

             🔑 In practice the softness only shows at maximum zoom-in - at normal play zoom a
             16-tile creature is well under 1,024 px on screen. That is why this ships rather
             than blocking. Do not read it as the rule being wrong.

             Life stages keep their original proportions throughout: x1.843 then x2. -->
